---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Base
  title="Lutaro - Support"
  description="How to get help with Lutaro: email the developer, or open an issue. Includes what to send when a camera will not connect."
>
  <h1>Support</h1>
  <p>
    Lutaro is made by one developer. Both routes below reach the same person -
    pick whichever you prefer.
  </p>

  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="mailto:lutaro@akitaka.me">lutaro@akitaka.me</a> - questions, bug
    reports, and requests for a camera Lutaro does not support yet. Email is
    the right route if you would rather not post in public, or if you are
    sending a diagnostics report.
  </p>

  <h2>Issue tracker</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="https://github.com/tarakanof/Lutaro-Site/issues">github.com/tarakanof/Lutaro-Site/issues</a>
    - public, and the better place for anything other users may hit too.
  </p>

  <h2>If your camera will not connect</h2>
  <p>
    Send a diagnostics report. The app builds it on your device from a small
    log of recent connection events, and it answers most of the questions a
    reply would otherwise have to ask.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>iPhone and iPad:</strong> Settings &rsaquo; Diagnostics &rsaquo;
      Prepare Report, then choose <em>Email to the Developer</em> in the share
      sheet. The report is attached for you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Mac:</strong> Settings &rsaquo; Diagnostics &rsaquo; Export
      Diagnostics, then attach the saved <code>.zip</code> to an email.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Reports are redacted by default - network addresses and serial numbers are
    masked. Only send a full-details report if I ask for one. Nothing is sent
    anywhere until you tap Send yourself; see the
    <a href={`${base}/privacy/`}>privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Asking about a camera</h2>
  <p>
    Check the <a href={`${base}/compatibility/`}>compatibility list</a> first.
    If your body is not on it, the most useful thing you can send is the
    <em>Check Camera Compatibility</em> report from the same Diagnostics
    screen, taken while the camera is connected - it says exactly which
    Picture Profile data that body exposes.
  </p>
</Base>
